From 3e08fb485a84ed826f2f70a6c9fe7028bfe83bb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:14:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [AESinkPipewire] Set the volume of the output device

Kodi scales its own samples for the volume, so other programs playing on
the same device, a web page for one, keep their own level and ignore
Kodi's volume keys, and quiet playback loses resolution before the
converter.

Provide a device volume through the sink factory: set a named device's
volume and mute with Kodi's gain curve and leave the scaling to
PipeWire. A card's sink takes them on the route its profile device is
on, where PipeWire drives the card's own mixer, as pipewire-pulse does;
any other sink takes them in its node's Props. The default device is not
tracked, so it has a volume control only when it is the one device
there is.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
